          %h3#OriginalArticles Original articles
          %p The development and use of string diagram calculus pre-dates its graphical appearance in print, due to the difficulty of printing non-text elements at the time.
          %blockquote
            %p Many calculations in earlier works were quite clearly worked out with string diagrams, then painstakingly copied into equations. Sometimes, clearly graphical structures were described in some detail without actually being drawn: e.g. the construction of free compact closed categories in Kelly and Laplaza’s 1980 “Coherence for compact closed categories”.
            %p
              (
              %a{:href => "http://angg.twu.net/categories-2017may02.html#.1"}> Pawel Sobocinski, 2 May 2017
              )
            %p This idea that string diagrams are, due to technical issues, only useful for private calculation, is said explicitly by Penrose. Penrose and Rindler’s book “Spinors and Spacetime” (CUP 1984) has an 11-page appendix full of all sorts of beautiful, carefully hand-drawn graphical notation for tensors and various operations on them (e.g. anti-symmetrization and covariant derivative). On the second page, he says the following:
            %p “The notation has been found very useful in practice as it grealy simplifies the appearance of complicated tensor or spinor equations, the various interrelations expressed being discernable at a glance. Unfortunately the notation seems to be of value mainly for private calculations because it cannot be printed in the normal way.”
            %p
              (
              %a{:href => "http://angg.twu.net/categories-2017may02.html#.2"}> Alex Kissinger, 2 May 2017
              )
          %p The first formal definition of string diagrams in the literature appears to be in
          %ul
            %li#Hotz65
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G%C3%BCnter+Hotz"}> Günter Hotz
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Eine Algebraisierung des Syntheseproblems von Schaltkreisen
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://www.magentacloud.de/lnk/LiPMlYfh"} part I
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://www.magentacloud.de/lnk/YivslUWJ"} part II
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/HotzSchaltkreise.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p
            Application of string diagrams to
            = succeed "-calculus" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor"} tensor
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mathematical+physics"} mathematical physics
            (hence for the case that the ambient
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal category
            is that of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+dimensional+vector+spaces"} finite dimensional vector spaces
            equipped with the
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product+of+vector+spaces"} tensor product of vector spaces
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Roger+Penrose"} Roger Penrose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/physics"} physicists
            know string diagrams as
            = succeed ":" do
              %em Penrose notation for tensor calculus
          %ul
            %li#Penrose71a
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Roger+Penrose"}> Roger Penrose
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Applications of negative dimensional tensors
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://www2.math.uic.edu/~kauffman/Penrose.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/PenroseNegativeDimensionalTensors.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
            %li#Penrose71b
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Roger+Penrose"}> Roger Penrose
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Angular momentum: An approach to combinatorial spacetime
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Quantum Theory and Beyond
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/PenroseAngularMomentum71.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
            %li#Penrose72
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Roger+Penrose"}> Roger Penrose
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em On the nature of quantum geometry
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Magic Without Magic
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://inspirehep.net/record/74082"} spire:74082
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/PenroseQuantumGeometry.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
            %li#PenroseRindler84
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Roger+Penrose"}> Roger Penrose
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wolfgang+Rindler"} Wolfgang Rindler
                = succeed "," do
